{% extends '@layout/blog-post.html.twig' %}

{% block body %}
<a title="Dotkernel PHP Formatter" href="http://www.dotkernel.com/download/?did=34" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Here</a> is  uploaded the XML file , ready to be imported in your Zend Studio, version 9.x

This file follow Dotkernel’s Coding standard.

Unzip the file.
Go to Zend Studio -&gt; Preferences -&gt; PHP -&gt; Code Style -&gt; Formatter
Import the xml file.

<h2 id="user-content-faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<div class="faq-list">
    <details class="acc" open>
        <summary>What is this file for? <span class="chev">+</span></summary>
        <div class="acc-body">
            <p class="mb-0">It is an XML file, downloadable from the linked page, that can be imported into Zend Studio (version 9.x) to set up the PHP code formatter so it follows Dotkernel's coding standard.</p>
        </div>
    </details>
    <details class="acc">
        <summary>How do I import the formatter file into Zend Studio? <span class="chev">+</span></summary>
        <div class="acc-body">
            <p class="mb-0">Unzip the downloaded file, then in Zend Studio go to Preferences -&gt; PHP -&gt; Code Style -&gt; Formatter and import the XML file.</p>
        </div>
    </details>
</div>
